# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# tracks — onboarded 2026-10-17 at James's tracks#1 (the repo was music-miles)
#
#   "Can you onboard these projects onto kit even if you don't start working
#   on them yet" … "I am kind of thinking just call it "Tracks" with a tag line
#   of track your tracks tracks"
#
# The repo was empty at onboarding, so there was no code to infer from. Everything here comes
# from what he has written on tracks#1: a running app that puts the music
# you listened to onto the route you ran. He renamed the repo to tracks on 2026-10-17, and
# the corpus follows it.
#
#   DEFINED   — his words on tracks#1. Cites the issue.
#   INFERRED  — my reading of the idea, or a detail it needs that he hasn't
#               stated. Each is `review unreviewed`: it shows in Proposed, and
#               he can deny it. Some lean on the Gemini reply he pasted there,
#               which he has not endorsed line by line.
#
# Nothing is built. The first slice is tracks#2 (scaffold) and tracks#3 (BEH-MAP-1/2/3).
#
# 2026-10-17, his steer on tracks#3:
#
#   "Let's not worry about the track visuals for now the main focus is we need
#   to be able to identify when the user has finished a Strava run and identify
#   which songs they have been listening to … This will require Strava and
#   Spotify integration … This will probably create kit backend specs"
#
# So FEAT-SYNC below is the priority, and the visual behaviours (BEH-MAP-1,
# BEH-SHARE-1) drop to priority 3 until he says otherwise.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

feature FEAT-BRAND "Name and voice"
feature FEAT-SYNC "Noticing a finished run and the songs played during it"
feature FEAT-CONNECT "Connecting Strava and Spotify"
feature FEAT-MAP "The music map of a workout"
feature FEAT-SHARE "Sharing a workout"


# ═══ DEFINED — tracks#1 ═══

behaviour BEH-BRAND-1 "The app is called Tracks, and its tagline is: Track your tracks' tracks"
  in FEAT-BRAND
  layer ux
  source defined tracks#1
  review unreviewed
  priority 1
  actor runner
  when opens page:Home
  then sees region:Hero
  contract "just call it "Tracks" with a tag line of track your tracks tracks": a running track, a GPS track and a music track
  contract unreviewed because he wrote "kind of thinking"; the name and the repo rename stay his


# ═══ DEFINED — tracks#3 (his steer) ═══

behaviour BEH-SYNC-1 "Tracks notices when a runner has finished a Strava run"
  in FEAT-SYNC
  layer technical
  source defined tracks#3
  review unreviewed
  priority 1
  actor runner
  contract "identify when the user has finished a Strava run": Strava pushes a webhook event when an activity is created, so Tracks listens rather than polls
  contract the subscription handshake echoes hub.challenge only when hub.verify_token matches the configured token; any other token is refused
  contract an event counts only when it is an activity create for a connected athlete; updates, deletes and athlete events are acknowledged and ignored
  contract the event is acknowledged at once and processed after, because Strava expects a reply within 2 seconds and retries otherwise
  contract a retried or duplicated event for the same activity is processed once
  contract only runs count (sport types Run, TrailRun, VirtualRun); a ride or a swim is ignored. Unreviewed: the list is my guess

behaviour BEH-SYNC-2 "Tracks identifies the songs the runner listened to during that run"
  in FEAT-SYNC
  layer technical
  source defined tracks#3
  review unreviewed
  priority 1
  actor runner
  contract "identify which songs they have been listening to": read the runner's Spotify recently-played history for the run's time window
  contract a song counts when its play overlaps the window from the run's start to its start plus elapsed time
  contract Spotify's played_at is taken as the moment the play ended, so a play spans played_at minus the track's duration up to played_at. Unreviewed: unverified against real data, so recheck it once his account is connected
  contract recently-played returns at most the last 50 plays, so the history is read as soon as the run is noticed, not later
  contract songs are returned in the order they played; a run with no songs in its window gives an empty list, not an error

behaviour BEH-SYNC-3 "Each finished run is kept with its songs, so the latest one can be fetched"
  in FEAT-SYNC
  layer technical
  source inferred tracks#3
  review unreviewed
  priority 1
  actor runner
  contract GET /api/runs lists the runs Tracks has noticed, newest first, each with the songs from BEH-SYNC-2
  contract unreviewed because the store is in memory until there is a database: a restart forgets runs, and a database is his call

behaviour BEH-SYNC-4 "The home page lists each noticed run with the songs played during it"
  in FEAT-SYNC
  layer ux
  source inferred tracks#3
  review unreviewed
  priority 1
  actor runner
  when opens page:Home
  then sees region:Runs
  contract a plain list, newest run first: its name, date and elapsed time (GET /api/runs carries no distance yet), then its songs in the order they played (title and artist)
  contract no map and no cover-art visuals, per "let's not worry about the track visuals for now" on tracks#3
  contract with no runs yet, it says so and explains a run appears after the next one finishes on Strava
  contract unreviewed because the layout and the fields shown are my guess


# ═══ INFERRED — what the idea needs ═══

behaviour BEH-CONNECT-1 "A runner connects their Strava account so Tracks can read their workouts"
  in FEAT-CONNECT
  layer ux
  source inferred tracks#1
  review unreviewed
  priority 1
  actor runner
  when opens page:Connect
  when activates button:ConnectStrava
  then sees region:Workouts
  contract read-only: Tracks never writes to Strava unless BEH-SHARE-2 is approved

behaviour BEH-CONNECT-2 "A runner connects their Spotify account so Tracks can read what they listened to"
  in FEAT-CONNECT
  layer ux
  source inferred tracks#1
  review unreviewed
  priority 1
  actor runner
  when opens page:Connect
  when activates button:ConnectSpotify
  then sees region:Workouts
  contract read-only: Tracks reads listening history and never controls playback

behaviour BEH-MAP-1 "Each workout shows the songs played during it, pinned along its route"
  in FEAT-MAP
  layer ux
  source inferred tracks#1
  review unreviewed
  priority 3
  actor runner
  given workout:WithSongs
  when opens page:Workout
  then sees region:RouteMap
  then sees region:SongList
  contract each song sits on the map at the point where it started, shown by its cover art
  contract the list below the map shows the same songs in order, with the distance each one covered

behaviour BEH-MAP-2 "A song is placed on the route by matching when it played to where the runner was"
  in FEAT-MAP
  layer technical
  source inferred tracks#1
  review unreviewed
  priority 1
  actor runner
  contract a song belongs to a workout when it started between the workout's start and end
  contract its pin is the route point whose timestamp is nearest the song's start
  contract a workout with no songs in its window still shows its route, with no pins

behaviour BEH-MAP-3 "A workout recorded without GPS lists its songs but draws no map"
  in FEAT-MAP
  layer ux
  source inferred tracks#1
  review unreviewed
  priority 2
  actor runner
  given workout:Indoor
  when opens page:Workout
  then sees region:SongList
  contract treadmill and indoor workouts have time but no route, so songs are listed by elapsed time

behaviour BEH-SHARE-1 "A workout can be saved as a share card: the route with the song covers on it"
  in FEAT-SHARE
  layer ux
  source inferred tracks#1
  review unreviewed
  priority 3
  actor runner
  given workout:WithSongs
  when opens page:Workout
  when activates button:Share
  then sees region:ShareCard
  contract sized for an Instagram or Strava story, from the Gemini reply he pasted
  contract minimal and high-contrast: the word TRACKS, the route line, the covers

behaviour BEH-SHARE-2 "The songs can be written into the Strava activity's description"
  in FEAT-SHARE
  layer technical
  source inferred tracks#1
  review unreviewed
  priority 3
  actor runner
  contract only when the runner turns it on: it is the one write Tracks would make to Strava
